{"reference":"Proverbs 27","book":"Proverbs","chapter":27,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"Reading Proverbs 27:5-6","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"These verses are concise, context-sensitive sayings rather than exceptionless rules. Their juxtaposition contrasts open rebuke and a friend’s painful honesty with the abundant kisses of an enemy, directing attention to the difference between words that are genuinely faithful and words that merely sound pleasant.","verse_refs":["Proverbs 27:5-6"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_proverbs_027_62a128c369989dadecf59cca"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}